---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import ModernHeader from '../components/ModernHeader.astro';
import ModernFooter from '../components/ModernFooter.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="AI Research Pillars in Zanzibar | SAAIL Lab · IIT Madras Zanzibar"
	description="Deep learning, machine learning, computer vision, and Swahili NLP research pillars at SAAIL Lab, IIT Madras Zanzibar, Tanzania: Precision Agriculture AI, Swahili Provenance, Responsible AI Governance, and Healthcare AI."
	canonical="https://saaillab.github.io/research/"
>
	<ModernHeader currentPage="research" />

	<main id="main-content">
		<section class="page-hero">
			<div class="container">
				<span class="page-eyebrow">Scientific Methodology &amp; Benchmarks · Zanzibar, Tanzania</span>
				<h1 class="page-title">Four Scientific AI Pillars Grounded in East Africa</h1>
				<p class="page-lead">
					Whereas active grants live under <a href="/projects/" class="hero-inline">Projects</a> and codebases under <a href="/github/" class="hero-inline">GitHub</a>, this page synthesizes the deep learning architectures, computer vision benchmarks, Swahili NLP pipelines, and clinical machine learning methods developed at IIT Madras Zanzibar.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="section">
			<div class="container pillars-stack">
				<!-- Pillar 1: Agriculture & Blue Economy -->
				<article id="agriculture" class="pillar-panel">
					<div class="panel-header panel-agri">
						<div class="panel-header-inner">
							<span class="panel-index">Pillar 01</span>
							<h2>Precision Agriculture &amp; Coastal Blue Economy</h2>
							<div class="panel-tags">
								<span>CashewAI</span>
								<span>Zanzibar Cloves</span>
								<span>Seaweed &amp; Blue Economy</span>
								<span>CropGuardNet</span>
								<span>Ubora-AI Mobile Grading</span>
							</div>
						</div>
					</div>
					<div class="panel-body">
						<p class="panel-intro">
							Smallholder commodities across East Africa lose value to unstandardized manual inspection, marine heatwave bleaching, and field disease pressure. Our vision architectures enforce foreground-grounded interpretability and leak-free deduplication so accuracy on held-out laboratory splits transfers safely to edge hardware.
						</p>

						<div class="pillar-visual-grid">
							<figure class="pillar-figure">
								<img src="/images/papers/cropguardnet/architecture.png" alt="CropGuardNet lightweight CNN-Transformer architecture" loading="lazy" />
								<figcaption><strong>Unified Edge Architecture:</strong> CropGuardNet compresses multi-scale dilated convolutions and a 2-head ViT into 481,574 parameters (63.8M FLOPs, 5.00 ms CPU ONNX).</figcaption>
							</figure>

							<div class="pillar-table-card">
								<h3>Verified Empirical Highlights</h3>
								<div class="table-scroll">
									<table class="pillar-table">
										<thead>
											<tr><th>System / Venue</th><th>Dataset Scope</th><th>Key Result</th></tr>
										</thead>
										<tbody>
											<tr><td><strong>CropGuardNet</strong> (Under Review)</td><td>35,420 unique images · 8 crops</td><td>99.17% acc · 0.9874 F1-macro · 200 FPS ONNX</td></tr>
											<tr><td><strong>Compositional XAI</strong> (ETRI 2026)</td><td>4,603 ZSTC clove buds</td><td>99.45% macro-F1 · 100% EER by design</td></tr>
											<tr><td><strong>CLOVES-4603</strong> (CVPR V4A 2026)</td><td>4 commercial clove grades</td><td>99.67% ResNet-50 · 92.94% texture SVM</td></tr>
											<tr><td><strong>ZSTC-Clove-V1</strong> (EAC STI 2026)</td><td>1,000 field-captured Zanzibar buds</td><td>96.50% test acc · 85.42% Grade 2 F1</td></tr>
										</tbody>
									</table>
								</div>
							</div>
						</div>

						<div class="panel-actions">
							<a href="/papers/cropguardnet/" class="btn btn-primary">CropGuardNet Paper</a>
							<a href="/papers/clove-xai-etri2026/" class="btn btn-secondary">ETRI 2026 Clove XAI</a>
							<a href="/projects/ubora-ai/" class="btn btn-secondary">Ubora-AI Project</a>
							<a href="/projects/seaweed-blue-economy/" class="btn btn-secondary">Seaweed Blue Economy</a>
						</div>
					</div>
				</article>

				<!-- Pillar 2: Language AI, Swahili Corpus & Dira Provenance -->
				<article id="language" class="pillar-panel">
					<div class="panel-header panel-lang">
						<div class="panel-header-inner">
							<span class="panel-index">Pillar 02</span>
							<h2>Swahili NLP, Provenance &amp; Culturally Attuned Models</h2>
							<div class="panel-tags">
								<span>Zanzibar Swahili Corpus</span>
								<span>Dira Provenance Benchmark</span>
								<span>Spoken Agricultural QA</span>
								<span>CARA-FM (PMLR 302)</span>
							</div>
						</div>
					</div>
					<div class="panel-body">
						<p class="panel-intro">
							Public African language evaluations rely heavily on machine-translated English text ("translationese") and compute footprints incompatible with offline mobile hardware. We build native Kiunguja Swahili text and spoken corpora paired with stylometric provenance detectors and low-memory foundation model agendas.
						</p>

						<div class="pillar-visual-grid">
							<figure class="pillar-figure">
								<img src="/images/projects/swahili_corpus_sources.png" alt="Zanzibar Swahili Corpus document counts and Swahili-dominant share" loading="lazy" />
								<figcaption><strong>Zanzibar Swahili Corpus Profiling:</strong> Native document counts and Swahili-dominant shares across regional sources anchored in coastal Kiunguja usage.</figcaption>
							</figure>

							<div class="pillar-table-card">
								<h3>Language &amp; Resource Targets</h3>
								<div class="table-scroll">
									<table class="pillar-table">
										<thead>
											<tr><th>Research Track</th><th>Target Reality / Scope</th><th>Core Scientific Focus</th></tr>
										</thead>
										<tbody>
											<tr><td><strong>Zanzibar Swahili Corpus</strong></td><td>Kiunguja text &amp; spoken audio</td><td>Domain-grounded coastal agricultural &amp; civic QA</td></tr>
											<tr><td><strong>Dira Provenance Detector</strong></td><td>Native vs. MT Swahili</td><td>Discriminating human writing from translationese</td></tr>
											<tr><td><strong>CARA-FM</strong> (PMLR Vol. 302)</td><td>1-4 GB RAM · &lt;500 MB CPU</td><td>4 pillars, 9 evaluation indices &amp; East African crop readiness</td></tr>
										</tbody>
									</table>
								</div>
							</div>
						</div>

						<div class="panel-actions">
							<a href="/projects/swahili-dira/" class="btn btn-primary">Swahili Corpus &amp; Dira Project</a>
							<a href="/papers/cara-fm/" class="btn btn-secondary">CARA-FM Paper (PMLR 302)</a>
							<a href="/datasets/#language" class="btn btn-secondary">Language Datasets</a>
						</div>
					</div>
				</article>

				<!-- Pillar 3: Responsible AI, Deployment Audits & Sovereign Governance -->
				<article id="responsible" class="pillar-panel">
					<div class="panel-header panel-resp">
						<div class="panel-header-inner">
							<span class="panel-index">Pillar 03 · 2x DLI Best Poster</span>
							<h2>Responsible AI, Evaluation Audits &amp; Regional Governance</h2>
							<div class="panel-tags">
								<span>DGS-Bench (DLI 2026)</span>
								<span>ICLR 2026 DDR</span>
								<span>DSA 2026 Kampala</span>
								<span>Oxford TAIS 2026</span>
								<span>AAAI 2026 Sovereignty</span>
							</div>
						</div>
					</div>
					<div class="panel-body">
						<p class="panel-intro">
							High accuracy on imbalanced agricultural datasets often masks silent minority-class collapse and capture-session confounding, whereas imported governance codes misfit regional institutions. Our audits formalize balanced evaluation metrics and anchor East African AI policy in Ubuntu, Harambee, and Ujamaa principles.
						</p>

						<div class="pillar-visual-grid">
							<figure class="pillar-figure">
								<img src="/images/papers/dgs2026/fig_multiseed_dgs.png" alt="DGS-Bench multi-seed evaluation mirage boxplots and 40/40 scatter across accuracy and macro-F1" loading="lazy" />
								<figcaption><strong>Exposing the Evaluation Mirage:</strong> Across 40 controlled runs (DLI 2026 Best Poster), raw accuracy implies false field improvement (-6.00 pp DGS), whereas macro-F1 exposes severe minority degradation (+8.16 pp).</figcaption>
							</figure>

							<div class="pillar-table-card">
								<h3>Auditing &amp; Policy Findings</h3>
								<div class="table-scroll">
									<table class="pillar-table">
										<thead>
											<tr><th>Study / Venue</th><th>Audit Target</th><th>Key Quantitative Finding</th></tr>
										</thead>
										<tbody>
											<tr><td><strong>DGS-Bench</strong> (DLI 2026 Best Poster)</td><td>iCassava 19,397 field images</td><td>Raw acc mirage in 40/40 runs; GrabCut bg drop 20-35 pp</td></tr>
											<tr><td><strong>DCGAN Failure</strong> (DSA 2026 Oral)</td><td>Extreme scarcity (n = 25-100)</td><td>DCGAN degrades ResNet-50 by -35.9 pp vs. real data</td></tr>
											<tr><td><strong>AgriAI Bias Card</strong> (DSA 2026)</td><td>PlantVillage vs. iCassava/iBean</td><td>Rubric scores 4/10 (PV) vs. 9/10 (African field sets)</td></tr>
											<tr><td><strong>Policy Harmonization</strong> (TAIS 2026)</td><td>Ethiopia, Kenya &amp; Rwanda</td><td>4 shared pillars across water, power, languages, council</td></tr>
										</tbody>
									</table>
								</div>
							</div>
						</div>

						<div class="panel-actions">
							<a href="/papers/dgs-bench/" class="btn btn-primary">DGS-Bench Paper</a>
							<a href="/papers/ai-policy-harmonization-tais2026/" class="btn btn-secondary">Oxford TAIS 2026</a>
							<a href="/projects/responsible-ai-global-south/" class="btn btn-secondary">Responsible AI Project</a>
						</div>
					</div>
				</article>

				<!-- Pillar 4: Healthcare & Clinical AI -->
				<article id="healthcare" class="pillar-panel">
					<div class="panel-header panel-health">
						<div class="panel-header-inner">
							<span class="panel-index">Pillar 04</span>
							<h2>Healthcare &amp; Clinical AI</h2>
							<div class="panel-tags">
								<span>PlacentaVision</span>
								<span>Preterm Serum Biomarkers</span>
								<span>BAFNet Polyp Seg. (ESWA 2025)</span>
							</div>
						</div>
					</div>
					<div class="panel-body">
						<p class="panel-intro">
							Low-resource maternity wards and diagnostic clinics require calibrated morphometric pipelines and sharp anatomical boundary fidelity without heavy compute servers. Through multi-institutional partnerships in Pemba, Penn State, and Zhejiang/Hangzhou, we advance non-invasive placental analysis and clinical segmentation.
						</p>

						<div class="pillar-visual-grid">
							<figure class="pillar-figure">
								<img src="/images/projects/placentavision_pipeline.png" alt="PlacentaVision automated three-view placental analysis framework" loading="lazy" />
								<figcaption><strong>PlacentaVision Pipeline:</strong> View-specific fetal, maternal, and trimmed placenta segmentation paired with calibration-ruler morphometry across 9,883 clinical photographs.</figcaption>
							</figure>

							<div class="pillar-table-card">
								<h3>Clinical Consortium Benchmarks</h3>
								<div class="table-scroll">
									<table class="pillar-table">
										<thead>
											<tr><th>Clinical Workstream</th><th>Cohort / Benchmark</th><th>Verified Outcome</th></tr>
										</thead>
										<tbody>
											<tr><td><strong>PlacentaVision Consortium</strong></td><td>9,883 bedside placental images</td><td>98.92% automated mask QC pass rate (9,776 valid)</td></tr>
											<tr><td><strong>CPHK Pemba Cohorts</strong></td><td>Zanzibar &amp; Pemba maternal serum</td><td>SHAP-explainable preterm &amp; neonatal risk models</td></tr>
											<tr><td><strong>BAFNet Segmentation</strong> (ESWA 2025)</td><td>EndoScene · CVC-ColonDB · ETIS</td><td>0.914 EndoScene Dice in 5.98M params (3.59 GFLOPs)</td></tr>
										</tbody>
									</table>
								</div>
							</div>
						</div>

						<div class="panel-actions">
							<a href="/projects/placentavision/" class="btn btn-primary">PlacentaVision Project Site</a>
							<a href="/papers/bafnet-polyp-2025/" class="btn btn-secondary">BAFNet Paper (ESWA 2025)</a>
						</div>
					</div>
				</article>
			</div>
		</section>
	</main>

	<ModernFooter />
</Layout>

<style>
	.hero-inline {
		color: var(--accent-primary);
		font-weight: 600;
		text-decoration: underline;
		text-underline-offset: 2px;
	}

	.pillars-stack {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 2.5rem;
	}

	.pillar-panel {
		background: var(--bg-card);
		border: 1px solid var(--border-color);
		border-radius: 1.15rem;
		overflow: hidden;
		box-shadow: 0 6px 20px var(--shadow-light);
	}

	.panel-header {
		padding: 1.85rem 2.25rem;
		color: #ffffff;
	}

	.panel-agri { background: linear-gradient(125deg, #0d3b22 0%, #14532d 100%); }
	.panel-lang { background: linear-gradient(125deg, #451a03 0%, #92400e 100%); }
	.panel-resp { background: linear-gradient(125deg, #0c1a12 0%, #1e3a2f 100%); }
	.panel-health { background: linear-gradient(125deg, #0f2d38 0%, #115e59 100%); }

	.panel-index {
		display: inline-block;
		font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
		font-size: 0.78rem;
		font-weight: 700;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		letter-spacing: 0.08em;
		opacity: 0.9;
		margin-bottom: 0.45rem;
	}

	.panel-header h2 {
		font-size: clamp(1.45rem, 2.5vw, 1.95rem);
		margin-bottom: 0.85rem;
		color: #ffffff;
	}

	.panel-tags {
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		gap: 0.45rem;
	}

	.panel-tags span {
		font-size: 0.76rem;
		font-weight: 600;
		padding: 0.22rem 0.68rem;
		border-radius: 999px;
		background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.24);
		color: #ffffff;
		border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.32);
	}

	.panel-body {
		padding: 2rem 2.25rem;
	}

	.panel-intro {
		font-size: 1.02rem;
		line-height: 1.72;
		color: var(--text-secondary);
		margin-bottom: 1.6rem;
	}

	.pillar-visual-grid {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.05fr) minmax(0, 0.95fr);
		gap: 1.65rem;
		align-items: start;
		margin-bottom: 1.75rem;
	}

	.pillar-figure {
		margin: 0;
		background: #ffffff;
		border: 1px solid var(--border-color);
		border-radius: 0.85rem;
		padding: 0.85rem;
	}

	.pillar-figure img {
		width: 100%;
		height: auto;
		max-height: 290px;
		object-fit: contain;
		border-radius: 0.5rem;
		background: #ffffff;
	}

	.pillar-figure figcaption {
		margin-top: 0.65rem;
		font-size: 0.84rem;
		line-height: 1.5;
		color: #475569;
	}

	.pillar-table-card {
		background: var(--bg-secondary);
		border: 1px solid var(--border-color);
		border-radius: 0.85rem;
		padding: 1.15rem 1.25rem;
	}

	.pillar-table-card h3 {
		font-size: 0.95rem;
		color: var(--accent-primary);
		margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
	}

	.table-scroll {
		overflow-x: auto;
	}

	.pillar-table {
		width: 100%;
		border-collapse: collapse;
		font-size: 0.85rem;
		text-align: left;
	}

	.pillar-table th {
		padding: 0.5rem 0.55rem;
		border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border-color);
		color: var(--text-primary);
		font-weight: 700;
	}

	.pillar-table td {
		padding: 0.55rem 0.55rem;
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-color);
		color: var(--text-secondary);
		vertical-align: top;
	}

	.pillar-table tr:last-child td {
		border-bottom: none;
	}

	.panel-actions {
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		gap: 0.75rem;
	}

	@media (max-width: 920px) {
		.pillar-visual-grid {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
		}
	}

	@media (max-width: 680px) {
		.panel-header, .panel-body {
			padding: 1.4rem;
		}
	}
</style>
